From: <webmaster@rapidcow.org>
Date: Tue, 18 Mar 2025 12:30:00 -0500
Subject: Planned Update

[%- IF html -%]
[%   SET dots = '&hellip;' -%]
[%   SET begin_it = '<em>' -%]
[%   SET end_it = '</em>' -%]
[% ELSE -%]
[%   SET begin_it = '*' -%]
[%   SET end_it = '*' -%]
[%   SET dots = '...' -%]
[% END -%]
[% BLOCK it %][% begin_it %][% content %][% end_it %][% END -%]

[% IF html %]<p>[% END -%]
Hello Netizens.  It's been a while I know.  I don't have
much to say except CS400 sucks...  I haven't got the
time to do anything.  I am barely handing in my other
homework because everything snowballed ever since I had
to review three other people's code. (And if you are the
one person who has seen the sole code review I have ever
written, you'll know why I never got to complete just
one review.)
[%- IF html %]</p>[% ELSE %]
[% END -%]

[% IF html %]<p>[% END -%]
Thank goodness it is just about to be over and I will have
some time to roast about their abysmal course structure.
Hopefully it won't ambush me with the next project or
something like that (which is about making Web and GUI
applications which, I'm not particularly excited about.
As long as they don't force us to use anything monolithic
or expect us to squeeze everything in one class I should
be... relatively fine.)
[%- IF html %]</p>[% ELSE %]
[% END -%]

[% IF html %]<p>[% END -%]
I will be putting the goodies on www.endfindme.com though
(which is perfect for keep the angry "dry" boring stuff out
of my main web sites, but not quite "impersonal" enough to
be managed by someone else's domain/web server ;) since they
seem to want us to "submit" the next project's stuff through
the CSL user pages at pages.cs.wisc.edu/~user/.  Their
submission model has always been sketchy as heck since they
stopped using the tested-and-tried Gradescope, but I'll rant
about all that in one go.  Also, I use the word "submit" even
though I've yet checked the relevant course instruction pages
if that is the medium through which they want us to present
our work.  I just happened to stumble upon an impressive
array of student-made "web sites" the other day I was
navigating the public course directory in the CSL Ubuntu
machine.  They are like a graveyard of dead HTML pages that
served one purpose (that was likely the same reason that
brought them here) and ceased to be useful since.  With the
chilling wind blowing through tombtones, engraved with the
names of their previous owner, once eminating beams of life,
now hauled indifferently into the abyss, and trapped in this
bleak directory of nowhere.  The files that live on in this
strange kind of limbo but will never become what it was,
carrying nothing but the temporary memories and bits it
survived for...
[%- IF html %]</p>[% ELSE %]
[% END -%]

[% IF html %]<p>[% END -%]
Sorry, I am simply inclined to say such stuff about the
copius amounts of code and other things they had us write,
but will never have a second chance to see the light of the
day.  It saddens me to see that this is the way things are
in school assignments, in proprietary code bases (from what
I've heard).  How people could write stuff only to part with
it for good.  Of course my concern is less about the stuff
they wrote because they're, uh, trash anyways. :D
But I don't like that happen to [% WRAPPER it %]my[% END %] code.  My code [% WRAPPER it %]is[% END %] my
voice... and I don't like being trapped.  Which is kind of
the whole reason I make web sites, instead of trying to get
a proper Instagram account and follow every person I've
interacted with.  (Or a YouTube channel where I yap about
stuff as I know everything... that sounds fun, sure. &gt;_&gt;)
[%- IF html %]</p>[% ELSE %]
[% END -%]

[% IF html %]<p>[% END -%]
~RC (since it's been a while, I'll do a proper sign-off...)
[%- IF html %]</p>[% ELSE %]
[% END -%]

[% IF html %]<p>[% END -%]
P.S. Yes, I do have YouTube, and I do still have an idea
of what I want to upload.  But I will do that sparingly
since they now have AI video summaries, and... you know.
I want the context stuff on my web site and treat YouTube
more like a CDN than a self-contained source of truth.
There is <a target="_blank" href="https://indieweb.org/POSSE">an IndieWeb wiki page</a> about this.
[%- IF html %]</p>[% ELSE %]
[% END -%]
